            <ArticleTitle>Convulsion after blood transfusion in four beta-thalassemia intermedia patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>549-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Four children with beta-thalassemia intermedia ages 7 to 11 years developed a clinical picture characterized by headache, hypertension, convulsion, and cerebral hemorrhage after blood transfusion. Successive transfusions did not result in a similar picture. Factors responsible for this syndrome are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
